// Settings for the small editors Sublime embeds in its chrome: the find and
// replace inputs, the command palette's input, the console.
//
// No "color_scheme" key here, which is the point. Adaptive does the same: with
// nothing specified the widgets fall through to the window's own color scheme,
// so they take Oxide's background and syntax colours instead of Sublime's
// stock widget theme. Sublime looks this file up by the active theme's name,
// so it must be "Widget - Oxide" to pair with Oxide.sublime-theme.
{
    "draw_shadows": false
}
